WEBVTT

00:00:01.330 --> 00:00:05.631
'Collective' is a distribution claim, and the benchmark disagrees.

00:00:05.631 --> 00:00:08.976
Public Agent Skills, compiled into RL environments.

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:18.117
7,971 containerised RL environments compiled from 3.4k public Agent Skills.

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:22.952
Adding the rubric, against outcome-only RL.

00:00:22.952 --> 00:00:25.553
−4.0 points on Terminal-Bench.

00:00:25.553 --> 00:00:28.154
−3.0 on S2EBench pass.

00:00:28.154 --> 00:00:30.755
−11.5 on S2EBench score.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.823
Skill-alignment preference test, against the base model.

00:00:35.823 --> 00:00:39.271
Outcome-only, 54.5%; with the rubric, 73.0%.

00:00:39.271 --> 00:00:43.294
One seed, one judge model, 300 steps.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:49.107
Collective preference and benchmark pass rate are measurably not the same objective.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:56.358
Every number here is from the full article, with its sources, at ai.thesatyajit.com.
